#!/bin/bash
# memex — thin client for the memex HTTP daemon, called by the
# openclaw chat agent. Wraps POST /search and POST /index against the
# memex container reachable on the docker-internal network at
# http://memex:18790.
#
# Usage:
#   memex search <query> [limit]      # default limit 5, returns JSON
#   memex index <path>                # index a markdown file by path
#   memex health                      # quick liveness check
#
# Output is JSON. Pipe through `jq` for human reading. Errors land on
# stderr with a non-zero exit code.
set -euo pipefail

BRAIN_URL="${BRAIN_URL:-http://memex:18790}"
CMD="${1:-}"
shift || true

case "$CMD" in
  search)
    QUERY="${1:-}"
    LIMIT="${2:-5}"
    if [ -z "$QUERY" ]; then
      echo "memex search: <query> required" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    BODY=$(jq -nc --arg q "$QUERY" --argjson k "$LIMIT" '{q:$q,k:$k}')
    curl -fsS -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      --data "$BODY" "${BRAIN_URL}/search"
    echo
    ;;
  index)
    P="${1:-}"
    if [ -z "$P" ]; then
      echo "memex index: <path> required" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    BODY=$(jq -nc --arg path "$P" '{path:$path}')
    curl -fsS -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      --data "$BODY" "${BRAIN_URL}/index"
    echo
    ;;
  health)
    curl -fsS "${BRAIN_URL}/health"
    echo
    ;;
  ""|-h|--help|help)
    cat <<USAGE
memex — query the personal-knowledge brain.

Commands:
  search <query> [limit]   hybrid retrieve (default limit 5), prints JSON
  index <path>             read a markdown file and index it
  health                   liveness check on the memex daemon

Env: BRAIN_URL  override the daemon endpoint (default http://memex:18790)
USAGE
    ;;
  *)
    echo "memex: unknown subcommand '$CMD'" >&2
    exit 2
    ;;
esac
